builds are blocked by the old .NET 10 catalog pins. Bind the normally published and repository-signed Builds 4.44.14 at `979cfd3e2c4145be516fbd833dacfc6b8e8fdce5` and enable the named 1.7.x qualification/publication lane.\n\nThe exact tool pin, supported range floor, catalog gitlink/blob/hash and public archive/inventory identities now agree. Source publication requires both latest exact-source current/legacy qualification jobs and all five SDK jobs, with the actual executing workflow/source/run bound and rechecked before publication.\n\nThe genuine legacy source `3aa95205d54fc6daba229f38655a024ae88132f1` carries identical code, tests, helpers and documentation; only the original eight metadata paths differ. Its original 349 controls, tool/catalog/provenance and no-acceptance classification remain intact. The current 412-case profile is byte-identical to the supported base.\n\nValidation: all 19 tuple controls, 10 legacy controls and 42 source-release controls passed. The actual committed same-code comparison and normal published-artifact verifier (`--require-recorded`) passed, including the NuGet repository signature and exact executable version/source. Locked dependency signatures, complete commit messages and actual maintenance version analysis passed.\n\nHosted PR and merged-source current/legacy qualification and all five SDK gates are still required. This maintenance change grants no caller/native acceptance, current-cohort registration or Story 2.10 qualification.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Touches release qualification gates and producer/tuple metadata that block publication if wrong; changes are mostly CI, docs, and guarded dispatch logic with new tests.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> This PR **rebinds the Platform maintenance tuple to signed Builds `4.44.14`**, raising the module-tool pin, supported range floor in `hexalith-platform.json`, and all recorded identities in `eng/builds-tuple.json` (producer SHA, catalog blob/hash, archive, tooling, inventory). Matching doc sections in `README.md` and related guides document the new producer facts and move `4.44.13` to historical. `eng/legacy-tuple-source.json` records a new same-code legacy source revision for regression.\n> \n> To unblock **1.7.x consumer maintenance**, CI workflows (`tuple-ci.yml`, `catalog-builder.yml`) now run on `1.7.x`. **Qualified source publication** gains a `workflow_dispatch` path on `1.7.x`: `source-release.yml` eligibility and SHA handling branch on dispatch vs main `workflow_run`, `gate.mjs` delegates to new `maintenance-gate.mjs` (binds dispatch run, approved base range, successful push CI on `1.7.x` for both qualification workflows), and `release.config.mjs` adds a `1.7.x` semantic-release branch. Coverage includes `maintenance-source-release.test.mjs` and updated legacy/workflow assertions.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit e1e8ccf5f51211fd5bd80259fbfd851b83513100. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-17T18:26:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T18:52:18Z","closed_at":"2026-11-17T18:52:15Z","merged_at":"2026-11-17T18:52:15Z","merge_commit_sha":"571c6c7b20eb6c28b5d9ec67de1f90f40537ce9c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"tinouit","id":183023925,"node_id":"U_kgDOCui5NQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183023925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinouit","html_url":"https://github.com/tinouit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinouit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinouit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinouit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinouit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github